{"t":"msg","chat":"m2main","parts":[{"type":"text","text":"The ocean is a vast, breathing blue, its surface a mirror that reflects the sky while hiding currents that circle the globe. From sunlit shallows teeming with life to the abyss's crushing silence, it sustains countless species and regulates Earth's climate in quiet, relentless ways. Yet for all its familiarity, the sea still guards mysteries—from uncharted trenches to ancient wrecks—that remind us how much we have yet to understand."}],"seq":474}
